    "summaries": [
      {
        "action_date": "2025-02-13",
        "action_desc": "Introduced in House",
        "text": "<p><strong>Reorganizing Government Act of 2025</strong><br/>&nbsp;<br/>This bill revives expedited congressional consideration of certain Presidential plans to reorganize the executive branch, expands permissible plan purposes, and changes the prohibitions on plan content.<br/>&nbsp;<br/>The bill reauthorizes through 2026 a currently expired authority that requires expedited congressional consideration of certain executive branch reorganization plans submitted by the President.&nbsp;<br/>&nbsp;<br/>The bill also expands the purposes for which such reorganization plans may be undertaken, to include</p><ul><li>reducing the number of federal employees;</li><li>eliminating unnecessary and burdensome rules, regulations, and other requirements; and</li><li>eliminating government operations that do not serve the public interest.</li></ul><p>The bill removes the following prohibitions on the contents of such plans:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>creating new executive departments or renaming existing executive departments;&nbsp;</li><li>abolishing or transferring executive departments or independent regulatory agencies or all of their functions; and</li><li>consolidating executive departments or independent regulatory agencies or all of their functions.</li></ul><p>The bill also adds a new prohibition on content, specifying that any such plan may not create a net increase in federal workers or expenditures.</p>",
        "update_date": "2026-01-21T23:55:26Z"
      }
    ]
  },
